      "lastReply": "Here is your story.\n\nSheru the tiger was tired of eating the same thing every day in the jungles of Ranthambore. One evening, a warm, spicy smell drifted over from a wedding in the nearby village, and his nose followed it all the way to a giant pot of biryani. He hid behind a banyan tree, watched the old cook layer rice and masala, and decided right there that he would learn to make it himself.\n\nHis first tries were a disaster. He burnt the rice, dropped in a whole fistful of chillies, and sneezed so hard that the monkeys fell out of their tree laughing. But Sheru kept going. A kind old cook named Rahim chacha, who was more amused than scared, began leaving him little lessons: soak the rice first, fry the onions till golden, and never, ever lift the lid too early.\n\nAfter many moons, Sheru finally got it right. The rice was fluffy, the saffron glowed, and the smell pulled every animal in the jungle to his cave. The deer came nervously, the monkeys came greedily, and even the grumpy old bear asked for seconds. From that day on, nobody feared Sheru's roar, because it only meant one thing: the biryani was ready. 🐯\n\n6:10 AM",
